title One on one
intro A Red player is dribbling toward you.
flip vertical

setup
  lineup 7v7
  player R-LF at 44, 40
  player B-CB at 30, 40
  player B-CM at 48, 50
  ball with R-LF

step
  caption You are the defender in blue. Watch what happens.
  label B-CB You

step
  caption Red dribbles straight at you, and a Blue teammate sprints back to help.
  R-LF to 33, 40
  B-CM to 40, 46
  ball with R-LF
  arrow from R-LF to B-CB
  arrow from B-CM to 36, 42
  duration 1100

step
  caption Stay on your feet and jockey back — your teammate arrives to help.
  R-LF to 31, 40
  B-CB to 28, 40
  B-CM to 34, 42
  ball with R-LF
  arrow from B-CM to R-LF
  duration 1100

question
  prompt Red is dribbling at you and a teammate is coming to help. What should you do?
  answer Stay on your feet and slow them down
  wrong Slide in to win the ball
  wrong Back off to your goal line
  wrong Turn and run to your goalie
  correct Stay on your feet.
  why A slide is one chance only. Miss it and Red is past you while you are on the ground. Standing up gives your teammate time to arrive.

question
  prompt Red breaks past you toward goal — is it time to slide?
  answer Yes, to block the shot
  wrong No, keep jogging beside them
  wrong No, only when you are tired
  wrong No, never slide
  correct Yes, to block the shot.
  why Slides are for emergencies, like blocking a shot. The rest of the time, feet on the ground win more balls.
